<script>
import StageTiles from 'crm/src/reports/lib/StageTiles.abide'
import stageTilesSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/StageTiles.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import stageTilesTestSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/StageTiles.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import summarizeStageSource from 'crm/src/reports/lib/summarizeStage.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="Publish a count the DOM cannot see">
        <Example
            id="publish-count"
            app="crm"
            title="`publishedBy(work, source, fields)` — a count your own code keeps"
            summary="Three tiles show the deals in one stage. The stage summary counts its own passes, and the test asserts one pass per switch."
            files={{
                'src/reports/lib/StageTiles.abide': stageTilesSource,
                'src/reports/lib/summarizeStage.ts': summarizeStageSource,
                'src/reports/lib/StageTiles.test.ts': stageTilesTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <StageTiles />
        </Example>

        <p>A recomputation writes nothing to the DOM, so no DOM count can see it. The module counts
            its own passes on a record under <code>globalThis.__HARNESS_WORK__</code>, the global
            <code>PUBLISHED_WORK_KEY</code> names. <code>measure</code> zeroes every published record
            when a case opens, and copies it into <code>work.published</code>, a
            <code>PublishedWork</code>, when it closes.</p>

        <p><code>publishedBy</code> reads one source back by the fields you expect. A source that
            published nothing reads as <code>null</code>, and a field the record does not carry
            throws, so a misspelled counter never reads as one that stayed at zero.</p>

        <p>The three tiles read one derived value, so the summary runs once however many tiles
            show it. Give each tile its own call and the test reports three.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
